{number: 120}
{title: The Love of God}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
The [Eb] love of God is greater far
Than [Ab] tongue or pen can [Eb] ever tell;
It goes beyond the highest star,
And [Bb7] reaches to the lowest [Eb] hell.
The guilty pair, bowed down with care,
God [Ab] gave His Son to [Eb] win;
His erring child He reconciled,
And [Bb7] pardoned from his [Eb] sin.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [Ab] love of God, how rich and pure!
How [Eb] measureless and [Bb7] strong!
It [Eb] shall forevermore endure
The [Bb7] saints' and angels' [Eb] song.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [Eb] hoary time shall pass away,
And [Ab] earthly thrones and [Eb] kingdoms fall;
When men who here refuse to pray,
On [Bb7] rocks and hills and mountains [Eb] call;
God's love, so sure, shall still endure,
All [Ab] measureless and [Eb] strong;
Redeeming grace to Adam's race—
The [Bb7] saints' and angels' [Eb] song.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Could [Eb] we with ink the ocean fill,
And [Ab] were the skies of [Eb] parchment made;
Were every stalk on earth a quill,
And [Bb7] every man a scribe by [Eb] trade;
To write the love of God above
Would [Ab] drain the ocean [Eb] dry;
Nor could the scroll contain the whole,
Though [Bb7] stretched from sky to [Eb] sky.
{end_of_verse}
